  "$comment": "Cross-client test vectors for src/core/rules/tide/state.ts and src/core/rules/tide/catch-fill.ts. ADR 003 \u00a74. AUTHORITY: the documented assembly rules - motion thresholds from `constants.ts` (|rate| < 0.05 m/h slack, < 0.15 m/h near-slack, else signed rising/falling), cycle progress as the fraction between the two bracketing PUBLISHED turns, and the rule of twelfths in its classic 1-2-3-3-2-1 form (a standard piece of seamanship, not an invention of this codebase). `dailyRange` is the spread between the highest and lowest candidate in range, where the candidates are the published turns plus the two interpolated endpoints; the range is only `published` when both extremes landed on published marks. Reimplemented independently over real NOAA predictions.",
